WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.912
On this slide, we are focusing on applied example: classify a temperature.

00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:09.752
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:16.007
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:16.007 --> 00:00:19.142
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:25.292
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:28.637
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:28.637 --> 00:00:33.817
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:39.572
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:44.992
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
